# XSH tcsetattr()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Tests that change attributes use a pseudo-terminal (XSI) as the terminal; the descriptor
# tests need none. Held output (output suspended with tcflow(), a byte written) makes
# the draining wait long enough to observe. Only flags and values every terminal supports
# (ECHO, ICANON, VMIN, VTIME) are compared after a change: the page lets unsupported
# requests be silently dropped. Not tested: the B0 effect on modem lines, an input speed of
# 0, EINVAL when nothing in a request can be honoured (no portable way to build such a
# request), and the effect when the structure was not derived from tcgetattr().
# Background tests run a child in a session of its own with the pseudo-terminal as its
# controlling terminal; how a terminal is acquired is implementation-defined, so a
# set-up that fails is UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.001
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       tcsetattr(TCSANOW) on a pseudo-terminal subsidiary returns 0 and
           tcgetattr() then shows ECHO cleared, set again, ICANON cleared, VMIN
           equal to 3 and VTIME equal to 7 as requested.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
           Only flags every terminal supports are compared (the page lets
           unsupported changes be dropped).
test       t/001-tcsanow-readback.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.002
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       After tcsetattr(TCSANOW) setting ECHO on a non-canonical pseudo-
           terminal, a byte written to the manager is echoed back to the manager;
           after tcsetattr(TCSANOW) clearing ECHO, the next byte is not echoed.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
           Echo in non-canonical mode is the ECHO flag of XBD 11.2.5.
test       t/002-immediate.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.003
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       tcsetattr() leaves the termios structure it is given unchanged,
           whatever the optional_actions value (TCSANOW, TCSADRAIN, TCSAFLUSH).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/003-const-arg.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.004
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       With output suspended and one byte written (so not transmitted),
           tcsetattr(TCSADRAIN) does not return and does not change the
           attributes; once output is restarted it returns 0 and the change (ECHO
           toggled) is in effect.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
           Suspension is made with tcflow(TCOOFF); if the held byte reaches the
           manager anyway the test is UNRESOLVED (tcflow has its own assertions).
timeout    40
test       t/004-tcsadrain.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.005
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       Input received but not read is still readable after tcsetattr(TCSANOW)
           but is gone after tcsetattr(TCSAFLUSH).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/005-tcsaflush.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.006
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       tcsetattr() with an optional_actions value that is none of TCSANOW,
           TCSADRAIN, TCSAFLUSH (-1, 7, 100, 12345) returns -1 with EINVAL.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/006-einval-action.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.007
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      1988
says       tcsetattr(-1) and tcsetattr() of a closed descriptor return -1 with
           EBADF.
test       t/007-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.008
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      required
since      1988
says       tcsetattr() of descriptors for a regular file, both ends of a pipe and
           /dev/null returns -1 with ENOTTY.
test       t/008-enotty-file.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.009
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       A change made through one descriptor of a pseudo-terminal subsidiary
           is still in effect, as seen through a second descriptor, after the
           first one is closed (ECHO cleared, ICANON cleared, VMIN equal to 4).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/009-persist.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.010
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#ERRORS/EINTR
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#RATIONALE
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       With output suspended and one byte written, tcsetattr(TCSADRAIN)
           waiting for the output is interrupted by a caught signal (no
           SA_RESTART) and returns -1 with EINTR.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
           The wait is made long by suspending output; if the call does not block
           the test is UNRESOLVED.
timeout    40
test       t/010-eintr.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.011
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2001
says       A process in a background process group (not orphaned) whose SIGTTOU
           is neither blocked nor ignored and which calls tcsetattr(TCSANOW)
           (toggling ECHO) on its controlling terminal is sent SIGTTOU (default
           action: stopped).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    40
test       t/011-bg-sigttou.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.012
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2001
says       A process in a background process group which calls tcsetattr(TCSANOW)
           (toggling ECHO) on its controlling terminal while SIGTTOU is blocked,
           and again while it is ignored, completes normally (returns 0), is not
           stopped and the change is made.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    60
test       t/012-bg-quiet.c

assertion  XSH.tcsetattr.013
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#ERRORS/EIO
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2001
says       A process in an orphaned process group, with SIGTTOU neither blocked
           nor ignored, which calls tcsetattr(TCSANOW) (toggling ECHO) on its
           controlling terminal gets -1 with EIO.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    40
test       t/013-orphan-eio.c
